+ * row the GL lines light, so no offset is needed. On GLES (a Mali-G52, checked on a device) the GL
+ * lines light the other row, so the quads move by a 1/64 px fraction: enough to decide the tie,
+ * too little to change any pixel that is not on an edge.
+ */
+auto LineTieBias() -> glm::vec2;
+
+/**
+ * @brief Draws line strips as quads (hard or anti-aliased edge), one instance per segment (projectM issue #682).
+ *
+ * Upload() a LineBatch, Begin() once for its transformation and viewport, then Draw() its strips.
+ * Other draws may run between Begin() and Draw(): Draw() binds its own program and buffers. The
